Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_refused_carve_moves_nothing`.

The defect: the carve pins its region as soon as the region has a page to give, before the ceiling
is asked. It reads as harmless, since the pin is set on every successful carve anyway, but a carve
the ceiling refuses then leaves a pinned region that owes an unpin nobody will make.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(run.unmoved_since(before), "a refusal moved something")`,
on a carve refused at a ceiling from an unpinned region.

diff --git a/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs b/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs
--- a/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs
@@ -614,10 +614,11 @@
     /// `kind` is recorded for [`spent`](Self::spent) and counted against every subtree the region
     /// is in.
     pub fn retype_object_page(&mut self, name: u64, kind: ObjectKind) -> Option<u64> {
-        let r = self.table.get(entry(name))?;
+        let r = self.table.get_mut(entry(name))?;
         if r.watermark >= r.pages {
             return None;
         }
+        r.pinned = true;
         if !self.charge(name, Counted::Object(kind)) {
             return None;
         }
